e - cabin fuse block c14 (7.5A, ignition-switched); moved from bulkhead B c14 2026-09-28 (the pump's ECU signal is A27)\nsp_5v (Splice): +5V at ECU A (A32 lead 18 AWG) - feeds sp_5v_bha before bulkhead A (c2, c39, c40 at 20 AWG), an 18 AWG trunk to sp_5v_b on ST185-B-cabin (broken off), crossover (a), and an 18 AWG link to sp_5v_2\nsp_5v_2 (Splice): +5V cabin loads off sp_5v - APS, cruise ladder, w210 (20 AWG each)\nsp_gndout (Splice): Gnd Out at ECU A (A24 lead 18 AWG) - feeds sp_gnd_bha before bulkhead A (c3, c41-c44 at 20 AWG) for the A loads only; loom B's sensors return to their own Gnd Out, ECU B22 (no A24-B22 tie in the harness)\nsp_sw12 (Splice): switched 12V bus - its B-side load (VSS feed on bulkhead B c20) is drawn on ST185-B-cabin (broken off); relay coil+ feeds come from sp_cp_sw12 inside the fuse box (ST185-CabinPower)\nsp_chassis (Splice): cabin chassis ground - ECU-B B25/B34 join it on ST185-B-cabin (broken off)","schematicPosition":{"x":4200,"y":0}},{"id":"n_aps","text":"APS PEDAL - folded in 2026-10-11 (harness-reconcile pass step 2, \"pedal is one cable in A-cabin\"): ST185-APS-Pedal.harness and its DT06-6S/DT04-6P inline mate (IX_APS) are retired; the BRZ e-throttle pedal's Sumitomo TS 025 plug is wired directly from this file. 5 of 6 pins (VC2, GND2, VC1, GND1, VPA1 -> A14) are ECU-A signals, wired straight from here; the 6th (VPA2 -> ECU-B B33) still breaks off to ST185-B-cabin (br_w39) since it's a B-letter signal - same crossover as before, just without the intermediate connector. Colours follow the former inline mate's. Run length to the pedal is still a placeholder (was 150 mm pedal-to-inline on APS-Pedal; now pedal-to-dash) - TBD, measure at the car.","schematicPosition":{"x":4440,"y":1800},"width":390}],"wireParts":[{"id":"wp_20_blk","partNumber":"EW-1C20-BLK","manufacturer":"generic","description":"WIRE, ELECTRICAL, 20 AWG, BLACK, ETFE (TEFZEL) INSULATED, 150 C, M22759/16 OR EQUIV","color":"Black","gauge":{"value":20,"unit":"AWG"}},{"id"